# Jira-to-Playwright Agent

When the user invokes **Jira-to-Playwright Agent** or asks to automate a Jira story into Playwright:

1. Load and follow `.cursor/skills/jira-to-playwright-agent/SKILL.md`
2. Execute STEPS 1–9 in order — do not skip framework inspection (STEP 5)
3. Write artifacts:
   - Prefer Playwright Test: extend `tests/ui/` or add `tests/ui/{STORY-KEY}.spec.ts` (+ page objects under `src/page-objects/` only when needed)
   - Use clear, descriptive `test()` titles and `test.step()` names (no `allure.tms`, no `TC-*` tags); optional functional `allure.tags(...)` only (e.g. smoke, regression)
   - `qa-report-{STORY-KEY}.md` when requested
4. Coverage gate: ≥95% before STEP 6
5. Heal loop: max 3 retries after Playwright Test
6. No hardcoded waits; reuse `src/page-objects` POM; no duplicate page objects
7. Reporting: Allure only (`npm run allure:generate`); CI Job Summary via `npm run ci:summary`
